<h3>Kinds of cards</h3>
<div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Concept</strong></td><td>A basic concept card.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Entity</strong></td><td>Proper nouns, service names, people's names, and so on.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Guide</strong></td><td>A phrase that contains concepts and entities — a how-to, like "do this with that".</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Maps / Labs</strong></td><td>Concept cards that cover the whole picture.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">Capture tip — leave the purpose behind</span>
    When capturing knowledge, always write <strong>the purpose after the # (hash)</strong>. This is so you can search for it later. Since you end up capturing things and never looking at them again, it is good to leave <strong>hints that future-you can reach through search</strong>. When you hand off an ingest as well, if you have it ask "why did you collect this / what are you trying to do", it takes that intent and connects and reasons with past research in the main vault.
</div>
